{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeMonodromyJordan","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeMonodromyJordan","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeDescentQuadratic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Complex.Basic"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.jordan_nilpotent_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.jordan_nilpotent_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L97-L110","doc":"**The Jordan block is genuine**: `σ ≠ i·id` at the monodromy point —\nwitnessed on the constant state at a descent point. With `jordan_sq_zero`,\nthe length-rule module at `q = i` is non-semisimple at EVERY rank: the T2\nfinding is universal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.exists_descent_point","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.exists_descent_point","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L89-L95","doc":"Every inhabited descent structure has a descent point: since the step\nnever fixes the rank, either `u₀` or `t u₀` is a descent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.jordan_sq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.jordan_sq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L70-L87","doc":"**`(σ − i)² = 0` at every rank** — the T2 Jordan-block relation, proved\non the length-rule module of ANY descent structure by pure algebra from\nthe all-ranks quadratic (`σ² = 2i·σ + 1` and `i² = −1`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.monodromyN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.monodromyN","kind":"def","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L66-L68","doc":"The nilpotent part of the monodromy action: `N = σ − i·id`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.eigenvalues_collide_at_monodromy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.eigenvalues_collide_at_monodromy","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L58-L64","doc":"**The channel eigenvalues collide at the monodromy point**: `q = −q⁻¹`\nat `q = i`. The e₊ eigenvalue `q` and the e₋ eigenvalue `−q⁻¹` of the\nmerged channel pair coincide — the general-rank source of the T2\nnon-semisimplicity and the T4 weight singularity at `q = i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.monodromy_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeGeneral.monodromy_h","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeMonodromyJordan.lean#L53-L56","doc":"At the monodromy point `q = i`, the Hecke parameter is `h = 2i`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}